on, as had been requested by their attorneys. Their neighbor William "Roddie" Bryan was sentenced to 35 years. All three men already are serving life sentences for their convictions in state court.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Their family of Gabby Petito yesterday announced a wrongful death lawsuit against police in Moab, Utah. They accused the Department of failing to properly investigate Petito`s domestic violence case and protect her. The lawsuit seeks $50 million in damages. Petito`s fiance Brian Laundrie admitted killing her in a notebook that was discovered near his body after he took his own life.\par \par \uc2 JONES: David McCullough, a bestselling author and renowned historian has died. He won a Pulitzer Prize in 1993 for his biography on President \uc2 Harry Truman\uc2 , and another nine years later for a biography on President John Adams. In 2006, McCullough was awarded the Presidential Medal of Freedom, the nation`s highest civilian honor. He passed away on Sunday at his home in Massachusetts, surrounded by his five children. David McCullough was 89 years old.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Meanwhile, members of the House returned to Washington this week to take up that sweeping economic and climate bill just passed along party lines in the Senate. It is one of many issues on the plate of House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 . Of course, she`s also been in the headlines recently for her trip to Taiwan. She met with its president and voiced ironclad support for the island nation`s democracy. The White House publicly backed the speaker`s right to make that visit. But the President made clear, top military officials did not believe it was wise to do so at this time.\par \par \uc2 And in the aftermath, China has responded aggressively, escalating military action in the region and stoking fears of a confrontation. So we have a lot to discuss this morning with Speaker Pelosi who`s joining us for her first interview since returning to Washington.\par \par \uc2 Speaker Pelosi,