 LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [07:00:17]\par \par \uc2 HODA KOTB, NBC NEWS ANCHOR: Good morning. Breaking overnight, on display in an attempted show of force to the world, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  front and center at Russia`s annual Victory Day parade. Delivering a message to the West while the devastating war in Ukraine rages on, dozens feared dead after an airstrike on a school. But support for Ukraine grows First Lady Dr. Jill Biden making a surprise Mother`s Day visit while U2`s Bono and the Edge put on a touching performance inside a Kyiv subway station. Complete coverage live from Ukraine and Moscow straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 Divided nation.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CROWD: My body, my choice.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Protests rage across the country over abortion rights, including sit- ins at the homes of several Supreme Court justices. The issue taking center stage on Capitol Hill this week as Americans on both sides await the high court`s final decision.\par \par \uc2 Soaring gas prices inching up overnight closing in on an all-time high with the busy summer driving season on the way. Is there any chance of relief? We`ll bring you the very latest. Mystery in paradise, questions swirling around the shocking deaths of three Americans at an exclusive five star resort in the Bahamas. A fourth hospitalized after becoming dangerously ill.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: It`s really hard to wrap your brain around.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Inside the search for answers just ahead.\par \par \uc2 Those stories, plus, that`s more like it. After a chilly spring, a major warm up in the works for tens of millions this week, Al will tell us where to expect record high temperatures starting today.\par \par \uc2 And striking it Rich.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Rich Strike is coming up on the inside. Oh my goodness.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Inside that astonishing come from behind victory at the Kentucky Derby that people are still talking about one of the longest shots ever, a horse not even in the field just one day earlier taking the crown.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I fell down the paddock when he hit the wire. I passed out. I`m so happy.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KOTB: So how did he pull it off? We`ll talk live with the man behind that victory today Monday, May 9th, 2022.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: From NBC News, this is Today with Savannah Guthrie and Hoda Kotb live from Studio 1A in Rockefeller Plaza.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Good morning. Good morning. Good to see you. It`s a Monday morning. We`re so happy you`re joining us. Willie is in. Savannah and Craig are both off. It`s a pretty good day to be in to work today.\par \par \uc2 WILLIE GEIST, NBC NEWS ANCHOR: I mean, we`ve got a good one. How about that Kentucky Derby on Saturday, absolute stunner, an 80 to one long shot coming out of nowhere to win horse racing`s most iconic event. Put it this way, if you placed a $10 bet on Rich Strike, you are $800 richer this morning. And you owe some of that good fortune to this man, trainer Eric Reed. We will chat with him live in just a bit. What a story not in the race at this time. Friday morning when you sat here, a late entry wins the derby at 80 to one.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: I think he said he was hyperventilating but wow what a great win. And by the way, guys, if you drive and you place the bet on that horse you might need some of that extra cash. The national average for a gallon of regular now stands $4.33 that`s just shy of the record and up 14 cents in just the past week alone. We`re going to have more on that in the live report straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 GEIST: Those numbers are shocking but we want to begin in Russia this morning. The nation marking Victory Day, the anniversary of the Soviet Union`s World War II defeat of Nazi Germany with a display today of military might meant to send a message to the world.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yes, it comes just hours after a very different kind of display. One of solidarity for Ukraine on Mother`s Day First Lady Dr. Jill Biden appearing with the First Lady of Ukraine in the western part of that country. We have it all covered. We`re going to start with NBC`s Keir Simmons in Moscow and we should point out that Russia is cracking down on journalists. They are limiting what reporters can say under threat of imprisonment. With that said, Keir, Good morning.\par \par \uc2 KEIR SIMMONS, NBC NEWS SENIOR INTERNATIONAL CORRESPONDENT: Hoda, Willie, good morning to you. According to the Russian government, 11,000 military marched through red square behind me there this morning. President Putin himself walking close to us was cheered by the invited guests his speech as uncompromising as ever.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 SIMMONS\uc2  (voice-over): This morning, Russia`s military men and women marching through The Red Square and in victory parades across Russia, the message unmistakable. For Donbass some soldiers chanted, referring to the region of eastern Ukraine, where fighting is now focused, addressing them, President Putin defiant.\par \par \uc2 [07:05:16]\par \par \uc2 You are fighting for your motherland, its future, he said, blaming the West for the conflict, and saying the death of each of our soldiers is a grief for all of us. Russia`s leader invoking the memory of World War II on this day marking victory over the Nazis, but not declaring victory in what he calls his special military operation.\par \par \uc2 (on camera): This is a patriotic day for Russia, but it`s rarely been held on a day like today. Every one of these men and women have colleagues in Ukraine. President Putin saying just a moment ago, some of them have come here straight from the fighting.\par \par \uc2 (voice-over): After he spoke, intimidating military hardware, tanks, even nuclear capable missiles rolling through Red Square, but this was a smaller parade than last year. And a planned flyover of fighter jets and bombers canceled at the last moment, because of the weather the Kremlin said. Looking on with his grandson, this man told me, victory will come. It cannot be otherwise. This woman saying the victory of 1945 will be repeated in 2022.\par \par \uc2 That is President Putin`s message too, following the parade, laying a wreath at the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier. And so far, polls suggest the majority of his people appeared to support him.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 SIMMONS\uc2 : And today`s parade was dripping in symbolism. Hoda, people will be looking closely for clues as to the Kremlin`s intention. But Hoda today, President Putin giving little away. Hoda?\par \par \uc2 KOTB: All right, Keir Simmons for us there in Moscow. Keir, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GEIST: Meanwhile, inside Ukraine, rescue crews remain at the scene of a deadly airstrike on a school in the eastern part of the country. This as First Lady Jill Biden made a surprise weekend visit to Western Ukraine. NBC`s Erin McLaughlin joins us from Kyiv. Erin, good morning.\par \par \uc2 ERIN MCLAUGHLIN, NBC NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Good morning, Willie. Dr. Jill Biden is meeting today with the president of Slovakia to thank Slovakia for its support for Ukrainian refugees, this after spending Mother`s Day in western Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 MCLAUGHLIN (voice-over): After crossing into western Ukraine, First Lady Jill Biden greeted her Ukrainian counterpart with a bouquet of spring flowers and a warm hug in a powerful Mother`s Day show of solidarity.\par \par \uc2 JILL BIDEN, FIRST LADY OF THE UNITED STATES: That it was important to show the Ukrainian people that this war has