rate Republican I spoke with last night said he plans to vote for the Democrats. So even if the Trump playbook works in the primaries, it`s still unclear if it will be successful this fall as well. Savannah?\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: All right, that`s the question. Jesse, thank you.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Turning now to the war in Ukraine, Russian forces unleashing a series of new attacks overnight. One of them aimed directly at that besieged steel plant in Mariupol where civilians remain hold up inside. NBC`s Erin McLaughlin joins us now with the very latest. Hey, Erin, good morning.\par \par \uc2 ERIN MCLAUGHLIN, NBC NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Hoda, good morning. Today, the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  announced its plan to phase out Russian oil imports as soon as possible really by the end of the year, as in all eyes are in Kharkiv at this point, where Ukrainian forces are working to clear the devastation left behind by Russian troops.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 MCLAUGHLIN (voice-over): On the outskirts of the northeastern city of Kharkiv, Ukrainian troops survey the death and destruction the Russians left behind after reclaiming control of at least 11 villages, according to Ukrainian authorities. Meanwhile, after three days traveling on what`s been described as the road from hell, buses of civilians finally arrived on safe Ukrainian territory from the devastated city of Mariupol.\par \par \uc2 More than 100 women and children, many thought they might never live to see this moment. For weeks, they were trapped inside the nuclear bunker of an old steel plant, the last Ukrainian stronghold of the besieged city, surrounded by Russian forces with no way out.\par \par \uc2 You might think of you can`t imagine how scary it is when you sit in the shelter in a wet and damp basement, which is bouncing, shaking, she says. Until the \uc2 U.N\uc2 . and Red Cross managed what seemed impossible, negotiating a break in the fighting just enough time for some to escape, but many were left behind. Fourteen-year-old Vova (ph) made it out with his mom and brother. But his father, a Ukrainian fighter is still in the plant. He spoke to NBC`s Matt Bradley.\par \par \uc2 MATT BRADLEY, NBC FOREIGN CORRESPONDENT: What did your father tell you when you left? What did he say to you?\par \par \uc2 MCLAUGHLIN (voice-over): He said we`d meet each other soon.\par \par \uc2 In Kyiv, Tuesday, the wives and mothers of the trapped Ukrainian fighters marched to President Zelenskyy office for help. Amidst reports Russian troops were storming the plant. The \uc2 ICRC\uc2  says it`s working to secure more evacuations.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS HANGER, COMMUNICATIONS FOR THE INTERNATIONAL COMMITTEE OF THE RED CROSS: You need to pass checkpoints. You need to talk to the parties to the conflict, things on the ground change by the minute. We have to remember this is an active conflict zone.\par \par \uc2 MCLAUGHLIN (on camera): What`s your message to someone who has been left behind?\par \par \uc2 HANGER: We have not forgotten the people in Mariupol in Azovstal. And we are working round the clock tirelessly to get people out wherever they are trapped.\par \par \uc2 MCLAUGHLIN (voice-over): With the plant once again being relentlessly bombarded hope of another rescue mission fades with each explosion.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 MCLAUGHLIN: Ukrainian officials say, four more evacuations are planned for the Mariupol area today although none from that besieged steel plant. Hoda?\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Where it`s needed most. All right, Erin McLaughlin for us there. Erin, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Craig is with us now on the money beat this morning. Good morning.\par \par \uc2 CRAIG MELVIN, NBC NEWS ANCHOR: Yes, money beat indeed. Savannah, Hoda, good morning. Good morning to you as well. From Wall Street to Main Street all eyes are on the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  today expected to announce another hike to interest rates aimed at driving down that 