rdenas (ph) worried about paying even more for his dream home in Nashville, motivating him and his family to secure their big purchase as soon as possible.\par \par \uc2 (on camera): How far did you have to stretch to make this new house happen?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: We had to put about 8 percent over asking price on an already very expensive house.\par \par \uc2 KENT (voice-over): Another rate hike would also bump up the price of car and adjustable rate loans again, and make paying off credit card debt even costlier. With a half point increase, a $5,000 balance would carry an additional $193 in total interest. And the rate hikes are expected to continue through the rest of this year, as the Fed tries to strike a delicate balance to get inflation under control.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 KENT: And for the savers out there, today`s expected high could be good news if you`ve got one of those high yield savings accounts. And of course, this comes as so many Americans are changing their spending habits just to manage those tight budgets with inflation. Our new NBC News morning console online poll found that six in 10 shoppers say they`ve decided not to purchase an item because it was too expensive, or they`re deciding to wait until the price goes down. Craig?\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: All right, \uc2 Jo Ling Kent\uc2  for us. Jo, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: All right, busy morning in the weather department, a whole big mess out there.\par \par \uc2 DYLAN DREYER, NBC NEWS METEOROLOGIST: It is. I mean, it`s very gray here in New York. It`s going to just be rainy to start off this day. But we are going to see a chance of bigger storms through the middle of the country. But let`s take you first into the Northeast where we do have rain extending from just west of Boston all the way back towards Buffalo includes New York City, Washington is a little bit gray this morning. We`ve got some heavy pockets of rain across New England as well.\par \par \