ing signs the pair may have been linked romantically.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 BROCK (voice-over): This morning, the plot thickens in this mysterious manhunt. Corrections Officer Vicky White now wanted herself after vanishing Friday morning from an Alabama jail with the murder suspect.\par \par \uc2 MATT KEELY, U.S. FEDERAL MARSHAL FOR NORTH ALABAMA DISTRICT: You shouldn`t try to approach either one of these individuals. We consider both of them a dangerous in all probability, both individuals are armed.\par \par \uc2 BROCK (voice-over): The warrant with White`s name on it charging her with permitting aiding the escape of the 6 foot 9, 270 pound, Casey White, no relation, who was already serving 75 years for a series of violent crimes and now was facing capital murder charges.\par \par \uc2 SHERIFF RICK SINGLETON, LAUDERDALE COUNTY, AL: I think we`re all shocked in the sheriff`s office. Vicky was an exemplary employee, 17 years of unblemished record.\par \par \uc2 BROCK (voice-over): On the same day she was set to retire, Sheriff Rick singleton laying out an unnerving series of events in which he says White who oversaw transportation at the jail arranged for multiple vans of inmates to be moved to the courthouse using two deputies in each car per protocol. Then breaking policy, White claim she was the only one left to take the suspects for a mental evaluation that was actually never booked. On top story, Tom Llamas pressing the Sheriff about a possible romance.\par \par \uc2 SINGLETON: We have not confirmed any relationship.\par \par \uc2 TOM LLAMAS, NBC NEWS ANCHOR: So Sheriff just to be clear, you have received information from other inmates that there was a relationship there.\par \par \uc2 SINGLETON: We have.\par \par \uc2 BROCK (voice-over): One woman who served time there expressing disbelief at the prospect of Vicky White`s voluntary involvement.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: She`s a great woman. I mean, she`s very nice. I mean, she 